  "body": "In [this specification](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/timers-and-user-prompts.html#dom-alert), about `window.alert`, the step 8 is \r\n\r\n> Optionally, pause while waiting for the user to acknowledge the message.\r\n\r\nAnd it describes `pause` as follows.\r\n\r\n> Some of the algorithms in this specification, for historical reasons, require the user agent to pause while running a task until a condition goal is met.\r\n\r\nBut I couldn't find any references about what that historical reasons were, to hold and block the whole program until the \"goal\" is met.\r\nAnyone who knows about this?",
